+  - 'L9 round 23, KILL RULE DISAMBIGUATED (operator-directed), still HONEST NULL
+    on level progress (2026-07-17, claude-fable-5,
+    results/outer_loop_round23_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json): resolves round
+    22''s kill_mechanism_caveat decisively -- the kill is CROSSING THE STATIC
+    VIEWPORT TOP MID-FLIGHT (screen row 0), NOT the -55 eye row. Two-point
+    proof: the ungrown gap float (prefix + R,R, no grow click) dies at exactly
+    world row 0 with the camera at (0,0), while round 22''s door-3 float died
+    at exactly world -48 with the camera at -48 -- same screen row, 48 world
+    rows apart; no eye exists at world 0. CORRECTIONS THAT FOLLOW: (1) round
+    22''s "camera hard-clamp at -48" is RETRACTED -- the camera recenters
+    after each settle to rest_row - 38.5 (up-gravity; verified rests
+    20.5/2.5/-3.5/-9.5 -> cams -18/-36/-42/-48 exactly) or rest_row - 28.5
+    (down-gravity), and simply never moves during flight; -48 was the camera
+    at the highest rest ever achieved (-9.5). (2) Round 16''s
+    "growing the pillar first makes the fall survivable" is mechanically
+    explained: a flight survives iff its landing rest lies within the CURRENT
+    static viewport; the grown structure provides an in-view rest (20.5), the
+    ungrown float''s natural rest (~-5..-1) is above the view top (0) ->
+    death. (3) ASCENT ARITHMETIC: next_rest >= prev_rest - 38.5. The first
+    rest above the -18..-12 slab is ~-51 (under the -54 floor, if live);
+    it needs prev_rest <= -12.5 vs best-achievable -9.5 -- the seal is a
+    ~3-PIXEL SHORTFALL, not a wall. Rung-gain attempts at the ladder top all
+    null (own-cell click, y=0 edge click, ACTION5, ACTION7, frame-blocked
+    slides). (4) Round 22''s c55-59 eye-free-channel lead is MOOT as framed
+    (eyes were not the killer) and worse under the corrected rule (its first
+    rest -77..-73 needs prev_rest <= -34.5). NEXT LEAD, sharply focused: find
+    ANY mechanism creating a rest between world -13 and -48 in an ascent
+    column -- one 6px rung (-15.5, the door cell) cascades the entire tower
+    open (rest -15.5 -> view -54 -> rest ~-51 -> cam ~-89.5 -> toggle row +
+    both upper switches clickable -> full cols0-5 shaft opening -> goal
+    drop). Untested candidates: down-gravity rests on structure cells placed
+    at the player''s row band before a flip; multi-column structure
+    geometries; door-open timing against a mid-flight player; and whether the
+    -54 floor exists live at c13-29.'
   - 'L5 (mapped in a PRIOR session, unsolved at the time, not banked then --
