 - 2026-07-15: Operational retrospective for milestone 2026.07.510 (Complete) -- 10 experiments used 275.1 minutes, including 2 compute-bound tasks. The compute-bound entries in the slowest-five set took 33.3 minutes for the registry-rotated ARC live-agent attempt and 18.72 minutes for the sealed GGUF CUDA canary; the supplied evidence does not identify phase-level causes. The locked task-conditioned GPU-idle indicator is false, and no concurrent multi-model task is identified, so no DualGPURunner miss is established. The highest-leverage tooling change is an incrementally updated, schema-validated reconciliation scaffold; estimated_time_savings_pct=20 is conditional on halving the 114.9-minute reconciliation workload; results/operational_retro_2026_07_510.json
 - 2026-07-16 [outer-loop]: Solved and banked ARC-AGI-3 `lf52` level 7 in round 14. Source audit found the prior structural-null search discarded every `fozwvlovdui_red` jump; although carriers truly cannot cross rail-free column 7, the red peg is a reusable leapfrog partner that carries the west plain peg across row 8. The 759-action L1-L7 sequence reached level 8 through real `offline_arcade` steps, passed `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` from a fresh environment, and passed five additional fresh reset/replay trials. Registry credit advanced from 6 to 7 reproduced levels (aggregate 178 to 179); evidence: `results/outer_loop_round14_lf52_probe_20260716.json`.
 - 2026-07-17 [outer-loop]: bp35 L9 round 22 (claude-fable-5, operator: "try solving the unsolved bp35 game levels") — no new level banked (frontier stays 8/9), but delivered the absolute-coordinate world map rounds 20-21 called for, via drift-free registration of public animation layers (83-action loop closure exact). Major corrections: the camera hard-clamps at world -48 and the historical "fly off the open top" deaths are actually ascents into a downward pillar-eye row at world -55 guarding every column c14-46; the tower top is real and physical with TWO previously unknown gravity switches (~y=-57, -81) plus the 8-block toggle row (never live-visible because of the clamp); switch consumption removes exactly its two cols0-5 border floors (cell-exact), and the six switch border pairs account for every floor in the cols0-5 shaft — fully consumed it is a designed continuous drop into the goal pocket; door carves and structure build/carry/crush rules measured cell-exact; native cells immune to all rewrites. The goal pocket's only air connection is the cols0-5 shaft and no live path into it exists under any mechanism found (three full click sweeps at three histories; maximal one-life interactable clear does not win). Honest structural null, mechanically grounded far beyond rounds 20-21; next leads recorded (door-column float-cap, any rest above the clamp would unlock the untested toggle row). Evidence: results/outer_loop_round22_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json (adversarial-verify clean); registry gotcha appended.
+- 2026-07-17 [outer-loop]: bp35 L9 round 23 (claude-fable-5, operator: "try the disambiguation experiment for eye-kill vs above-view-kill") — RESOLVED decisively: the ascent kill is CROSSING THE STATIC VIEWPORT TOP mid-flight (screen row 0), not the -55 eye row (two-point proof: identical screen-row-0 deaths at world rows 0 and -48 under cameras 48 rows apart). Round 22's "camera hard-clamp at -48" is retracted — the camera recenters to rest−38.5 (up) / rest−28.5 (down) after each settle and never moves during flight; -48 was merely the camera at the highest rest achieved (-9.5). Flight-survival law: a float survives iff its landing rest lies within the current static viewport — this also mechanically explains round 16's grow-first-survives observation. The L9 seal is now quantified as a ~3-pixel shortfall: the first rest above the slab (~-51) needs a prior rest ≤ -12.5 vs best-achievable -9.5; one 6px rung (the door cell at -15.5) would cascade the whole tower open (toggle row + upper switches clickable). Rung-gain attempts all null this round; focused next leads recorded. No new level (frontier stays 8/9). Evidence: results/outer_loop_round23_bp35_probe_l9_20260717.json (adversarial-verify clean); registry gotcha appended.
