st achievable rest is -9.5 (carry-ladder top beneath a door) -- a shortfall of about 3 pixels. Rung-gain attempts at the ladder top all null this round: clicking the player's own cell, edge-clicks at screen y=0 (targeting the boundary cell), ACTION5, ACTION7, and lateral slides (frame-blocked) leave the player at -9.5. (4) Round 22's cols 55-59 'eye-free channel' lead is moot as framed (eyes were not the killer) and worse in the corrected frame: the channel's first rest is at -77..-73, requiring a prior rest at or above -34.5. The updated frontier question: does ANY mechanism create a rest between world -13 and -48 in an ascent column (which would cascade: rest -15.5 -> view to -54 -> rest -51 -> camera about -89.5 -> the toggle row and both upper switches become clickable and the tower top opens)? The door cell at -15.5 is the natural candidate rung and everything tested so far refuses to make it one. Frontier stays 8/9; honest null on level progress, decisive positive on mechanism identification.",
